  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Country Programme Outcome (CPO) supports Brazil in strengthening its capacity to engage with the international labour standards system, including the ratification, application, and reporting of ILO Conventions. In a context of persistent labour market challenges and gaps in the effective implementation of labour rights, it promotes stronger institutional coordination and greater engagement of tripartite constituents in normative processes, contributing to improved governance and alignment with international frameworks.
The expected outputs include enhanced capacities of government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, and other stakeholders to participate in and support normative action, as well as strengthened mechanisms for the application and reporting of ratified conventions. These efforts are expected to improve compliance with international obligations, reinforce the integration of international labour standards into national policies and practices, and support more effective monitoring and implementation. Overall, the interventions will contribute to advancing fundamental principles and rights at work and strengthening progress towards decent work and social justice in Brazil.</narrative>
  </description>
